{"id":"CMSC389O","title":"Special Topics in Computer Science; The Coding Interview","department":"Computer Science","level":"Undergrad","credits":"1","description":"Prerequisite: Minimum grade of C- in CMSC216 and CMSC250; and permission of CMNS-Computer Science department.\n\nTechnical interviewing is a critical skill for acquiring internships and jobs. Students will gain a comprehensive, practical introduction to technical interviews. Students will be introduced to basic topics such as Big O and String Manipulation and later move into more complex topicssuch as Graphs and Dynamic Programming. Most in-class time will bespenton mock interviews to give real interview practice. The course facilitators are experienced in interviewing and have received internship/job offers from companies like Meta, Optiver, Bloomberg, Amazon, Apple, Microsoft, Databricks, Capital One, and more.","gradingMethods":null,"noLongerOffered":false,"removedTerm":null,"removedDetected":null,"terms":[{"term":"201801","sections":1,"seats":30,"openSeats":5,"waitlist":0,"instructors":["Thomas Goldstein"],"removed":false},{"term":"201908","sections":3,"seats":90,"openSeats":0,"waitlist":0,"instructors":["Thomas Goldstein"],"removed":false},{"term":"202001","sections":5,"seats":150,"openSeats":5,"waitlist":0,"instructors":["Thomas Goldstein"],"removed":false},{"term":"202008","sections":4,"seats":120,"openSeats":5,"waitlist":0,"instructors":["Thomas Goldstein"],"removed":false},{"term":"202101","sections":4,"seats":120,"openSeats":0,"waitlist":11,"instructors":["Thomas Goldstein"],"removed":false},{"term":"202108","sections":5,"seats":150,"openSeats":8,"waitlist":0,"instructors":["Thomas Goldstein"],"removed":false},{"term":"202201","sections":5,"seats":175,"openSeats":23,"waitlist":0,"instructors":["Thomas Goldstein"],"removed":false},{"term":"202208","sections":5,"seats":150,"openSeats":9,"waitlist":0,"instructors":["Thomas Goldstein"],"removed":false},{"term":"202301","sections":5,"seats":150,"ope